    "items": [
     {
      "pClass": "productdescription",
      "pText": "Dahi Handi is a figure climber modelled on the human pyramid formed during Janmashtami. Six stylised human figures in different colours stand on each other's shoulders, and children climb up the figures themselves rather than a rock wall or net. Short pegs on each figure act as hand and foot holds. The idea teaches children to find their own route and to climb with care. It suits ages 5 to 12. The base footprint is small, 2'2\" x 1'4\", with a safe play area of 8'2\" x 4'4\". Climbing, hanging and balancing build physical fitness, coordination, balance and critical thinking. It is part of our Wall Play collection. The galvanised pipe and moulded parts carry a 3-year warranty. Ask us for a quote."
     }
    ]
